<rtept lat="51.8284500000" lon="-1.4529010000">
<time>2025-08-08T09:26:20Z</time>
<name>Bridewell Farm to End</name>
<desc><![CDATA[Walk past the elegant Grade II Bridewell Farmhouse (date stone 1761) to a footpath post on the right-hand side, with barns on the left-hand side. 

Turn right at the footpath post, up a track which swiftly heads uphill a short distance and then levels out. Follow the hedge on the left-hand field edge until it turns away to the left. 

At this point, the tower of St Mary's is in clear view in the distance ahead of you. You continue straight ahead across the field in the direction of the tower, towards a hedge gap.

Go through the hedge gap and follow the path as it skirts round a farm on the right. The path leads you to a tarmac lane by the farm. Follow the lane back to St Mary's Church and the start of the walk.  ]]></desc>
<sym>Flag</sym>
<type>Marks</type>
<extensions>
<xstyle:fill>
<xstyle:color>ff0000</xstyle:color>
</xstyle:fill>
